485 4.4 Summary of Claims
486 Here, we briefly summarize key takeaways from this section. To 487 reiterate, the goal of AdaSplit is to improve SL, so that it can be488 come a competitive alternative to FL. Conventional SL methods 489 reduce on-client computation, which is a key bottleneck to FL, but 490 increase server-computation, communication overhead and often 491 achieve lower accuracy when compared to FL methods. AdaSplit is 492 designed to help alleviate these concerns. 493 Contribution: AdaSplit introduces the following ideas to SL: local 494 client gradients (sec 4.1), intermittent server training (sec 4.1), in495 frequent communication with smaller payloads (sec 4.2) and sparse 496 updates of the server model (sec 4.3). Next, sec 6 & 7 present results 497 to show that these ideas enable AdaSplit to i) preserve the low on498 client computation as other SL methods (the only shared aspect), 499 ii) reduce server (and hence, total) computation cost (sec 4.1), iii) 500 reduce communication cost (sec 4.2) and iv) improve collaboration 501 between clients, evident via better accuracy (sec 4.3).
